  "notes": "Source: Arizona College of Nursing 2026 Academic Catalog, BSN (SOC 29-1140) schedule of courses (pp. 13-15), valid 01/01/2026-12/31/2026, retrieved 2026-10-01 from https://arizonacollege.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/AZC_Catalog_BSN_20260101_No26_V1b.pdf; course-level prerequisites cross-verified against the official BSN Program Course Descriptions page (https://arizonacollege.edu/accredited-bsn-program/bsn-program-course-descriptions/, retrieved 2026-10-01). program_type professional-phase: the school's own site states 'The BSN degree program is divided into two parts: general education and core nursing.' The 50-credit general-education phase is NOT term-ordered in the catalog ('may take four semesters to complete'; delivered as 8-week courses; gen-ed credits earned at another accredited college may transfer in), so no invented semester assignment is made -- the 15 official gen-ed courses are carried as external_prereqs. This plan covers the nursing core professional phase (catalog Semesters 5-9, 70 credits) with the catalog's genuine term-by-term order. CORE GATE: every Semester-5 course lists the official prerequisite 'Admission to Core Nursing Program' (admission to the BSN program plus completion of all gen-ed coursework with required grades/GPA); this is an admission gate, not a course code, so it is documented here and not set as a machine prereq. PREREQ VERIFICATION: NUR 337's official prerequisite is NONE (per the BSN Program Course Descriptions page). NUR 443 requires the Semester-8 block (NUR 335/335L/336/336L/423/427/428, per the official course-descriptions page); the quality-sequence chain is NUR 338 -> NUR 358 -> NUR 428 -> NUR 448. EXCLUDED VARIANTS (not applicable to the UT/FL/MI campuses): the Colorado-only variant (47-credit gen ed, NUR 356L/335L/336L at 3 credits, 765 clinical hours) and the California-only nursing core schedule plus the LVN 30-unit option. The 0-credit AFS 100 Academic Foundations Seminar is not part of the official 120-credit schedule of courses and is excluded. PSC 101 is 'not applicable in Colorado' only and applies to these campuses. TITLE NOTE: catalog prints 'Leader in Quality Care & Patient Safety II/IV' but 'Leader in Quality & Patient Safety I/III' -- transcribed verbatim. SAME-PROGRAM: one shared catalog governs all campuses with no campus-level exceptions for Utah, Florida, or Michigan; the official catalog-calendar page lists Salt Lake City, Sarasota, and Southfield among the BSN campuses. This single plan serves all three; Sarasota and Southfield are recorded as same-program in their inventories. transfer_confidence core_only: private institution with no published TCCNS/articulation equivalencies; tccns mirrors the local course code. NOTE vs prior waves: earlier AZCN plans (Chesapeake/Hartford/St. Louis) distributed the flat 50-credit gen-ed list across invented Semesters 1-4; current iron rules forbid inventing term order, hence this professional-phase form.",
